  "question": {
    "text": "An aqueous solution of oxalic acid dihydrate contains its $6.3 \\mathrm{~g}$ in $250 \\mathrm{ml}$. The volume of $0.1 \\mathrm{~N}$ $\\mathrm{NaOH}$ required to completely neutralize $10 \\mathrm{ml}$ of this solution",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nEcdV",
      "text": "\n$4 \\mathrm{ml}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0a4B9",
      "text": "\n$20 \\mathrm{ml}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "W5IAQ",
      "text": "\n$2 \\mathrm{ml}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EFFjl",
      "text": "\n$40 \\mathrm{ml}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Normality of oxalic acid solution\n$$\n=\\frac{6.3 \\times 1000}{63 \\times 250}=0.4 \\mathrm{~N}\n$$\nNow from\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& N_1 V_1=N_2 V_2 \\\\\n& 0.4 \\times 10=0.1 \\times V_2 \\\\\n& V_2=40 \\mathrm{~mL}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
